# .Renviron.example
# Copy this to .Renviron and fill in the values you need. .Renviron is
# gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The app runs with NONE of these set: it falls back to the local data in
# data/schema/ and writes submissions to dev/submissions_local.csv.

# ---- Data source -------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the six star-schema CSVs are read from. Leave unset to use the local
# data/schema/ directory. In production, point it at the raw GitHub URL of the
# directory holding the CSVs, with NO trailing slash, so the client can publish
# new data without redeploying the app.
# FW_DATA_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ORG/REPO/main/data/schema

# ---- Submission backend ------------------------------------------------------
# "local" (default) appends to dev/submissions_local.csv. No credentials needed.
# "sheets" writes to the private review Sheet. NOT YET TESTED - see the README.
# FW_SUBMIT_BACKEND=local

# The submissions Sheet. Required only when FW_SUBMIT_BACKEND=sheets.
# FW_SHEET_ID=1AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz0123456789
# FW_SHEET_TAB=submissions

# The Google service account key, as the ENTIRE JSON on one line. Required only
# when FW_SUBMIT_BACKEND=sheets. Never point this at a file in the repository and
# never commit a real value. On Posit Connect Cloud this is set as a variable in
# the deployment settings, not in a file.
# FW_GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"REPLACE_ME","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nTHIS_IS_NOT_A_REAL_KEY\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"fwise-writer@example.iam.gserviceaccount.com"}
